===Vaultings===
*On [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/719509-new-items-are-entering-prime-vault/ November 15, 2016], it was announced that the Vasto Prime, alongside {{WF|Nova Prime}} and {{Weapon|Soma Prime}}, would enter the [[Prime Vault]] and be retired from the reward tables. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.
*Vasto Prime, along with {{WF|Mag Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}}, {{Weapon|Soma Prime}}, {{Weapon|Boar Prime}}, and {{Weapon|Dakra Prime}}, were [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/1027106-the-prime-vault-is-open/ unvaulted] from November 13th, 2018 to January 29th, 2019.
*From [https://www.warframe.com/news/trinity-and-nova-prime-vault May 26th, 2020] to [https://www.warframe.com/news/ember-and-frost-prime-vault September 29th, 2020], Vasto Prime emerged from the Vault along with {{WF|Trinity Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}}, {{Weapon|Dual Kamas Prime}}, and{{Weapon|Soma Prime}}.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Vasto Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Vasto Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*The Vasto Prime has a high chance of cutting corpses into pieces, making it ideal for a [[Desecrate|Desecrating]] {{WF|Nekros}} to bring along. The game considers corpses that have been bisected at the torso as separate entities, allowing Desecrate to convert '''both halves''' into individual chances for more drops.
*Due to Vasto's incarnon form using the burst trigger, it cannot benefit from [[Semi-Pistol Cannonade|Semi-Pistol Cannonade.]]

==Trivia==
*The Vasto Prime was one of the first Prime items which had colorable gold parts. This trait is shared with the {{Weapon|Soma Prime}}, {{WF|Nova Prime}}, [[Syandana#Prime_Access.2FVault_exclusives|Pyra Prime Syandana]], and several other primes.
*With the introduction of [[Damage 2.0]], the original {{Weapon|Vasto}}, along with {{Weapon|Akvasto}}, became able to cut enemies into pieces due to its overwhelming slash damage. The Vasto Prime inherited this trait.
*The Vasto Prime also bears a striking visual resemblance to the [https://guns.fandom.com/wiki/Joseph_Enouy Enouy Revolver].

